---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "HOA Fees and Mortgage Payment (How to model them)";
const description =
  "HOA dues are part of your housing payment. Learn how to model HOA fees, special assessments, and cash flow impact. Educational use only.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/hoa-fees-and-mortgage-payment">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">HOA fees</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>HOA fees and your mortgage payment</h1>
    <p>
      HOA dues are not part of your loan balance, but they do affect your monthly housing payment and DTI. This guide shows how
      to include them in your estimates and plan for special assessments.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How HOA affects payment</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>HOA dues are added to the housing payment for DTI calculations.</li>
      <li>They do not reduce principal, so they do not affect amortization.</li>
      <li>Fees can change yearly and may include special assessments.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What to confirm</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Monthly dues amount and how often they can change.</li>
      <li>What the HOA covers (insurance, maintenance, utilities).</li>
      <li>Any pending special assessments or reserve shortfalls.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Modeling steps</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Add the HOA monthly dues to your housing payment input.</li>
      <li>Use the total housing payment in DTI comparisons.</li>
      <li>Stress test with a higher HOA amount if increases are likely.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Documents to review</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>HOA budget, reserves, and recent financials.</li>
      <li>Master insurance policy coverage limits.</li>
      <li>Special assessment history and planned projects.</li>
      <li>Rules for dues increases or reassessments.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Leaving HOA dues out of the mortgage payment estimate.</li>
      <li>Ignoring special assessments that can raise monthly costs.</li>
      <li>Assuming HOA includes insurance when it does not.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>HOA increase history and any planned hikes.</li>
      <li>Reserve funding level and pending assessments.</li>
      <li>Items covered by HOA vs your own budget.</li>
      <li>Insurance coverage gaps between HOA and personal policy.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">How mortgage payments are calculated</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/principal-and-interest-vs-escrow">Principal and interest vs escrow</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Do lenders include HOA in DTI?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes, HOA dues are typically included in the housing payment used for DTI.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can HOA dues change after closing?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes. HOAs can raise dues or levy assessments, so keep a buffer for changes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Run the mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Affordability checklist</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-01-31</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
